# v2.35.0 — Sprint B coop-rewrite (V2 cooperative-tensor SHIP-BROAD)

**SHIP verdict**: BROAD — V2 wins across density [0.01, 0.50] by 1.96-13.53× vs SDPA+bias.

## TL;DR

Sprint B graduates from narrow niche (v2.34.0: density ≤ 0.01) to broad envelope.
Single-kernel cooperative-tensor inner-GEMM (V6NAX forward pattern adapted) replaces
the per-thread FA-2 of v2.34.0. V2 dominates SDPA+bias across the full density
sweep including moderate densities (FlashVSR-typical 0.07-0.24) and beyond.

## Public API

```python
from mlx_mfa.lcsa_nax import (
    sparse_attention_nax,           # V2 by default, V1 fallback for ineligible
    sparse_attention_dispatch,      # NAX route default (threshold 0.95)
    DEFAULT_DENSITY_THRESHOLD,      # 0.95 (was 0.02 in v2.34.0)
)
from mlx_mfa.integrations.flashvsr_lcsa import patch_flashvsr_lcsa
```

## Capabilities

- dtype: float16 (bf16 deferred — V1 fallback handles bf16 paths)
- head_dim ∈ {64, 128}
- block_tile = 32 (V2 eligibility; non-32 BT silently falls back to V1)
- mask ndim ∈ {2, 3, 4}
- All-False mask row → exact zero output (v2.34.0 contract preserved)

